# ── Generated pipeline data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Raw fetched files (API JSON, scraped HTML + manifests). Despite this ignore
# rule, the raw files that already exist are committed and tracked in git —
# this rule only blocks *new* files written by future `make ingest` /
# `make elections-ingest` runs from being auto-staged. That's deliberate: the
# committed raw/ tree is what lets the Render Docker build run `make
# pipeline-all` with no network access to StatFin or vaalit.fi at build time
# (see ARCHITECTURE.md §15 / CONTEXT.md §15). If you refresh raw data and want
# the new snapshot committed, use `git add -f` — and consider whether the old
# snapshot should be removed first, since nothing does that automatically.
backend/data/raw/

# Processed CSVs – generated by the transformation pipeline from raw data.
backend/data/processed/

# Analysis output – generated by run_analysis.py and generate_region_insights.py.
# region_insights/ alone can contain 300+ per-municipality JSON files.
backend/data/analysis/

# Reference data at backend/data/*.csv and *.json IS tracked (region_mapping.csv,
# party_mapping.csv, region_mapping.json). Only the subdirectories above are ignored.

